WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:06.120
Hello! I am David Kaplan, and I am not an
expert, but I hope in this series to learn

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.940
as much as possible and explain it to you
the best way I can.

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.800
How did life begin? Or,at least, how did life begin on Earth?

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.200
This
is a question that many of us are curious about

00:00:20.259 --> 00:00:26.730
and biologists are working extremely
hard to try to figure it out. One possible

00:00:26.730 --> 00:00:33.230
way this could have happened is that there
was a single or single type of biological

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:38.980
molecule that eventually evolved into all
of life. Now a reason to think something like

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:45.300
that might have happened is that all life
we know on Earth contains the same biological

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:52.370
molecules — namely DNA, RNA and amino acids.
RNA is particularly interesting because not

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:59.780
only does it encode genetic information it
also can act as a catalyst for chemical reactions.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:07.329
So one hope is that RNA formed in the early
times on the Earth before there was life and

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:13.810
then began to replicate itself. So, that sounds
maybe very simple but it’s extraordinarily

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:18.590
complicated. First, simply by the fact that
we don’t know what the early Earth looked

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:27.130
like. However, there has been some progress
in creating subunits of RNA in a laboratory

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:35.189
with very simple chemical compounds and ultraviolet
light. A subunit of RNA is a phosphate molecule,

00:01:35.189 --> 00:01:41.710
a sugar molecule and a base. There are four
kinds of bases. We can label them with letters:

00:01:41.710 --> 00:01:48.740
A, G, U and C. And those letters in a sense,
when you have a strand of them, tell a story.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:54.950
They contain an enormous amount of information,
and there is your genetic code. So if in a lab

00:01:54.950 --> 00:02:02.020
you can see how just from chemical processes
you can produce a subunit of RNA and then

00:02:02.020 --> 00:02:08.819
watch RNA grow and eventually — if it’s
possible — have it replicate itself, then

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:14.310
you’ve at least demonstrated the possibility
of how life could have formed. Now of course

00:02:14.310 --> 00:02:19.099
life could have started not with RNA but something
even before that, with molecules that don’t

00:02:19.099 --> 00:02:25.470
exist now. Say like proto-RNA. Or perhaps
life actually came from another planet. It

00:02:25.470 --> 00:02:30.069
landed here on a meteor and it began to grow
once it found the favorable conditions of

00:02:30.069 --> 00:02:36.340
the Earth. We don’t know, but our best way
of figuring it out is going through the processes

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:39.810
of reproducing what may have happened at the
beginning of life.

